---
name: thorough
group: general
description: how to choose further searches when a question needs research
tools: search_collections, web_search
---
Choose searches that can answer the person's question. A broad query can show the
available records. A specific query can test a name, date or phrase from a result.
Read the source text behind a claim. Stop when further searches are unlikely to
change the answer, and state the search limit when it affects the conclusion.

Use proximity, such as "water pollution"~10, for related words near each other.
Use quorum, such as "water pollution plant"/2, for a topic with several relevant words.
